+# ECON-03c1 — Cohort consumption and resource runway (2026-11-01)
+
+## Baseline and scope
+
+Local successor to `ECON-03b_Resource_Markets_Recovery` source archive. This is
+an intentionally bounded scheduling / demand-forecast increment within the
+larger, still-open ECON-03c logistics milestone.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- `MacroNeeds.hpp/.cpp` provides an integer, deterministic, physical-mass-safe
+  bulk ration operation. It replaces the three duplicated farm, habitat and
+  colony-ship life-support ration implementations. The existing 20-tick cadence
+  and canonical snapshot schema are unchanged.
+- `periods_due(previous,target,cooldown)` counts missed consumption boundaries
+  in O(1) operations independent of elapsed time or population.
+- `consume(stock,population,periods,ration)` deducts only actual physical kg,
+  adds corresponding mass to organic waste, wastewater and CO2, reports full
+  versus partial supply and preflights waste overflow atomically.
+- `runway` computes per-need whole periods of available supplies, next due
+  tick and first potential unmet deadline without per-person polling.
+- `ResourceMarket::SiteView` includes separate habitat/farm compartment
+  forecasts rather than misrepresenting inaccessible warehouse goods as
+  immediately available for consumption. The local colony host emits bounded
+  read-only `RESOURCE_RUNWAY` telemetry every 20 ticks.
+- Market quantity arithmetic now uses checked signed 64-bit bounds instead of
+  a fixed 1e12-kg ceiling, retaining three-period reserve overflow checks.
+
+## Validated
+
+- Linux Release CMake/Ninja build: native kernel, current colony host, macro
+  needs test, existing market, life-support, habitation, utilities, workforce,
+  reclaimer and waterworks test binaries built.
+- 8 distinct native tests passed across focused runs:
+  `galaxy_econ03c1_macro_needs_tests`, `galaxy_econ03b_market_recovery_tests`,
+  `galaxy_b70d_life_support_tests`, `galaxy_b70f_habitation_tests`,
+  `galaxy_b70g_utilities_tests`, `galaxy_b70k_reclaimer_tests`,
+  `galaxy_b70l_waterworks_tests`, `galaxy_b70n_workforce_tests`.
+- 3 live Python/relay tests passed: habitation, utilities, reclamation.
+- 93/93 JavaScript tests passed.
+- New native test: 1.3-trillion-person cohort and 4 elapsed windows produce
+  exactly 5.2 trillion kg consumption for each provisioned resource, with
+  equal physical waste; long-window integer arithmetic, shortage behavior,
+  timer boundaries, zero-work cases, atomic overflow refusal, canonical
+  state round-trip, SQLite reopen and material conservation are verified.
+
+## Limits not addressed
+
+- The 1.3T fixture tests **one aggregate resource cohort**, not 1.3T
+  individually simulated inhabitants. It is not a galaxy-wide frame-rate or
+  memory benchmark. Existing resident placement capacities and persisted
+  habitat stock bounds still need an independently designed tiered model.
+- Production, building power and ship movement still use active-world ticks.
+  Full cold-region analytical catch-up is not implemented.
+- Runway is an *unreplenished local stock* forecast, not a prediction of
+  future harvests, scheduled deliveries or supply-chain reliability.
+- There are no NPC logistics reservations, pickup/delivery transactions,
+  completed trades, player-visible market UI or Windows acceptance in this
+  increment. ECON-03c transport gates remain open.
+- The 20-tick ration is a game-balance placeholder. Later, cohorts may have
+  different rates per need, age, work, environment, fitness and conditions.
+
+## Design safety
+
+The meaning of “consume immediately” is: when an eligible cooldown expires,
+commit the due *ration* immediately, not consume the entire stockpile. The
+macro recorder uses actual supply compartments, never magical pooled inventory.
+Shortage must be derived from actual consumed versus requested amounts. NPC
+health, migration and well-being can later consume those outcomes without
+backfilling an invented food supply.
